21nh|n|In Old English, the article the, when the following word began with a vowel, was often written with elision as if a part of the word. Thus in Chaucer, the forms thabsence, tharray, thegle, thend, thingot, etc., are found for the absence, the array, the eagle, the end, etc.	n:xgy,61,4~xgy,61,4	N:1vbw,20,3;15k0,11,1~1vbw,20,3;15k0,11,1
